For each K the function takes the mean and standard deviation of the
estimated Ln probability of the data, LnP(K), over the replicate runs,
and computes LnP'(K) = LnP(K) - LnP(K - 1),
|LnP''(K)| = |LnP'(K + 1) - LnP'(K)| and
